course: dictionary
lesson: 12441
title: Decisive moments
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The sentences around it tell you which meaning the writer chose. Look for clues like who is doing the action, what the result is, and how sure everyone is.
explain: «Mia was decisive and picked the red bag in seconds.» Mia did not dither or ask lots of questions. She chose quickly and firmly, so decisive describes a person who makes choices fast and sure.
explain: «Scoring in the last minute was the decisive goal of the match.» Here decisive means the goal that changed the result. Without it, the score would have been different. Ask yourself: what would have happened without this?
explain: «The judge gave a decisive victory, with no doubt at all.» Now decisive means clear. Nobody could argue about who won. To check any meaning, put it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Decisive means able to make decisions quickly and firmly.
fact: Decisive also means having the biggest effect on the result, like «the decisive goal».
fact: Decisive can mean clear, with no doubt, like «a decisive victory».
fact: «Decisively» is the adverb: «The captain acted decisively and called the team together.»
fact: A «decisive moment» is the moment that settles what happens next.
exercise: «Mia was decisive and picked the red bag in seconds.» What does decisive describe here? | A colour of bag | A slow, tired walker | Someone who is very tall | *Someone who makes choices quickly and firmly
exercise: «Scoring in the last minute was the decisive goal of the match.» What does decisive mean here? | A goal that was not allowed | A goal that was very small | *The goal that had the biggest effect on the result | A goal scored in the first minute
exercise: Which word in «The team won a decisive victory» means clear, with no doubt? | team | won | *decisive | victory
test: «The captain acted decisively and the crowd cheered.» What does decisively mean here? | Sadly, looking at the ground | *Quickly and firmly, without hesitating | Angrily, shouting at everyone | Slowly, with many questions
test: Which phrase means the moment that settled the result? | a sleepy moment | a noisy moment | *a decisive moment
exam: Ali says decisive means slow and unsure. Which meaning is correct? | Full of doubt | *Able to decide quickly and firmly | Slow and unsure | Late and rude
